# App hub — new app pages

When the user asks to add a new app by name (or official/privacy pages under `apps/`):

1. Follow the full checklist in **`docs/ADD_APP_PLAYBOOK.md`** (naming, 8 files, 4 hub edits, forbidden root files).
2. Use **`en/apps/Houriva/`** (or `en/apps/CheckMED/`) as the HTML structure template: `canonical` / `hreflang`, `langSwitch` + `data-rel`, `../../../assets/`, theme FAB, three JS scripts.
3. **Root hub** (repo root `index.html`): link targets **`en/apps/<AppName>/...`**. **Locale hubs** `en/index.html`, `ko/index.html`, `ja/index.html`: link targets **`apps/<AppName>/...`** (relative to that locale folder).
4. **Do not** modify or delete: `app-ads.txt`, `CNAME`, `google39b438b48ece26d9.html`, `zzzindex.html` (see repo root `AGENTS.md`).
5. Omit Play Store badges/icons until URLs and assets exist; use “coming soon” / 준비 중 style copy like Houriva stubs.
